# Hibernate 6 and JPA 3.1 Migration Guide

## Overview
Spring Boot 3.x uses Hibernate 6.x as the default JPA provider, which comes with significant changes from Hibernate 5.x. Most applications will work with minimal changes, but there are important differences to be aware of.

## Major Changes in Hibernate 6

### 1. Jakarta Persistence API (JPA 3.1)
Hibernate 6 implements JPA 3.1, which uses `jakarta.persistence.*` instead of `javax.persistence.*`.

### 2. Improved Type System
Better handling of Java types and JDBC mapping.

### 3. Query Language Enhancements
HQL (Hibernate Query Language) has been improved with better syntax.

### 4. Performance Improvements
Significant performance enhancements in query execution and caching.

## Common Migration Issues and Solutions

### 1. Identifier Generation

#### Issue: @GeneratedValue Strategy Changes
In Hibernate 6, `GenerationType.AUTO` behavior has changed.

```java
// This works the same in both versions
@Id
@GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
private Long id;

// For MySQL/PostgreSQL, IDENTITY is preferred
// For Oracle, use SEQUENCE
@Id
@GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.SEQUENCE)
private Long id;
```

**Recommendation**: Use explicit strategies instead of AUTO.

### 2. @Type Annotation Removed

#### Old (Hibernate 5)
```java
@Type(type = "org.hibernate.type.NumericBooleanType")
private Boolean active;
```

#### New (Hibernate 6)
Use standard JPA annotations or custom UserType:
```java
// For most cases, just remove @Type - Hibernate 6 handles it
private Boolean active;

// For custom types, use @JavaType or @JdbcType
@JdbcType(NumericBooleanJdbcType.class)
private Boolean active;
```

### 3. Criteria API Changes

Most Criteria API code remains compatible, but some edge cases changed.

```java
// Standard Criteria API - no changes needed
CriteriaBuilder cb = entityManager.getCriteriaBuilder();
CriteriaQuery<User> query = cb.createQuery(User.class);
Root<User> root = query.from(User.class);
query.select(root).where(cb.equal(root.get("username"), username));
```

### 4. HQL Changes

#### Implicit Joins
