### 1. Lazy Loading Outside Transactions
```java
// This will fail with LazyInitializationException
@GetMapping("/users/{id}")
public User getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
    User user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    user.getOrders().size(); // ERROR: No transaction
    return user;
}

// Solution 1: Use @Transactional on controller method
@Transactional(readOnly = true)
@GetMapping("/users/{id}")
public User getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
    User user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    user.getOrders().size(); // OK
    return user;
}

// Solution 2: Fetch eagerly in query
@Query("SELECT u FROM User u LEFT JOIN FETCH u.orders WHERE u.id = :id")
Optional<User> findByIdWithOrders(@Param("id") Long id);

// Solution 3: Use DTOs (recommended)
public UserDTO getUser(@PathVariable Long id) {
    User user = userRepository.findById(id).orElseThrow();
    return new UserDTO(user); // Convert in transaction
}
```

### 2. N+1 Query Problem
```java
// BAD: Causes N+1 queries
List<User> users = userRepository.findAll();
for (User user : users) {
    System.out.println(user.getOrders().size()); // 1 query per user
}

// GOOD: Use JOIN FETCH
@Query("SELECT DISTINCT u FROM User u LEFT JOIN FETCH u.orders")
List<User> findAllWithOrders();
```

### 3. Cascading and Orphan Removal
```java
@OneToMany(
    mappedBy = "user",
    cascade = CascadeType.ALL,
    orphanRemoval = true
)
private List<Order> orders = new ArrayList<>();

// When removing from collection, orphanRemoval deletes the entity
user.getOrders().remove(order); // Order will be deleted from DB
```

## Testing with Hibernate 6

```java
@DataJpaTest
class UserRepositoryTest {

    @Autowired
    private UserRepository userRepository;

    @Autowired
    private TestEntityManager entityManager;

    @Test
    void testFindByUsername() {
        User user = new User("testuser", "test@example.com", "password");
        entityManager.persist(user);
        entityManager.flush();

        Optional<User> found = userRepository.findByUsername("testuser");

        assertTrue(found.isPresent());
        assertEquals("test@example.com", found.get().getEmail());
    }
}
```

## Performance Tips

1. **Use appropriate fetch types**: LAZY by default, EAGER only when always needed
2. **Enable batch fetching**: `spring.jpa.properties.hibernate.default_batch_fetch_size=10`
3. **Use query hints**: `@QueryHints(@QueryHint(name = "org.hibernate.cacheable", value = "true"))`
4. **Profile queries**: Enable `spring.jpa.show-sql=true` during development
5. **Use DTOs for read operations**: Avoid loading full entities when only few fields needed

## Migration Checklist

- [ ] Verify all `javax.persistence.*` imports changed to `jakarta.persistence.*`
- [ ] Review custom `@Type` annotations - remove or update
- [ ] Test all custom HQL/JPQL queries
- [ ] Verify identifier generation strategies
- [ ] Test lazy loading behavior
- [ ] Run full test suite
- [ ] Performance test critical queries

